ti-bandgap: downgrade the 'sensor is unreliable' message from warn to info.
OMAP3503 flags its bandgap UNRELIABLE; the warning appears on every boot and
the project treats boot-console warnings as defects. Cosmetic (log level only).
Rationale for the warn->info choice is inferred from the project's boot-console
rule, not from a comment in the tree.

--- a/drivers/thermal/ti-soc-thermal/ti-bandgap.c	2026-11-15 11:37:04.880901861 -0500
+++ b/drivers/thermal/ti-soc-thermal/ti-bandgap.c	2026-11-15 11:37:04.884902169 -0500
@@ -897,7 +897,7 @@
 	bgp->dev = &pdev->dev;
 
 	if (TI_BANDGAP_HAS(bgp, UNRELIABLE))
-		dev_warn(&pdev->dev,
+		dev_info(&pdev->dev,
 			 "This OMAP thermal sensor is unreliable. You've been warned\n");
 
 	if (TI_BANDGAP_HAS(bgp, TSHUT)) {
